// --- CONFIGURATION ---
// v is NORMALIZED to [0,1]: the real domain (phi in [0, PI/A]) depends on A,
// and the limits of the MESH_BEGIN sections are evaluated on the CPU by ExprTk
// WITHOUT the slider constants (extractMeshSections, mainwindow.cpp ~7630):
// writing "v: 0, PI/A" would not compile. The rescaling is done below in the shader.
u_min := 0;
u_max := 6.28318531;
v_min := 0;
v_max := 1;
steps := 400;

// --- HOPF FIBERS OVER THE SPIRAL theta = A*phi ---
// Same fibration h: S^3 -> S^2 as the "Hopf Tori over Parallels" presets, but
// the base curve is no longer a parallel theta = const: it is the LOXODROMIC
// SPIRAL theta = A*phi, which goes down from the north pole to the south pole
// winding around the axis. The lift of that curve is the surface.
//
// THE LIFT. With the Hopf tori convention (r = theta/2, i.e.
// |z1| = cos r and |z2| = sin r), the point above (theta, phi) with fiber
// parameter u is
//     z1 = cos(r) e^{i(phi + u)}      z2 = sin(r) e^{i u}      r = theta/2
// Substituting theta = A*phi gives r = A*phi/2. Verified to be a true
// lift: h is constant along u to 1e-16, and the base rebuilt from h has
// exactly theta = A*phi and phi_base = phi.
//
// WHY phi STOPS AT PI/A (and not at 2*PI). On the sphere the colatitude lives
// in [0, PI]: theta = A*phi leaves that range as soon as phi > PI/A. Letting
// phi run up to 2*PI the curve does NOT go on, it RETRACES: at A = 2 the points
// phi = 0 and phi = PI give r = 0 and r = PI, i.e. (cos r, sin r) = (1,0) and
// (-1,0) -- the SAME fiber C12 traversed twice. Measured: minimum distance
// between non-adjacent points = 0.0000, i.e. the surface self-intersects.
// With phi in [0, PI/A] the curve runs between the two poles ONCE and the
// surface is EMBEDDED for every A (minimum distance between non-adjacent points
// ~0.03-0.06, verified for A = 0.5, 1, 2, 4).
//
// CONSEQUENCE: it is NOT a torus, it is an ANNULUS (cylinder).
// The domain is [0, PI/A] x S^1 and the two edges are the two POLAR FIBERS:
//     phi = 0     -> |z2| = 0 -> the great circle C12 = {(cos u, sin u, 0, 0)}
//     phi = PI/A  -> |z1| = 0 -> the great circle C34 = {(0, 0, cos u, sin u)}
// (verified: |z1| and |z2| are 1 and 0 on the respective edges).
// The surface is therefore a BAND joining the two polar Hopf fibers,
// winding around the axis as many times as A says. The Hopf tori over
// the parallels are instead CLOSED because a parallel is a closed curve; a
// spiral going from pole to pole is an ARC, and its lift has a boundary.
// Every line v = const is still a FIBER, i.e. a great circle of S^3
// (measured: center at the origin to 2.5e-3, radius 1.000000) -- in stereographic
// projection a Villarceau circle. The wireframe along u shows them directly.
//
// A NEED NOT BE AN INTEGER. Closing up in phi (which would need an even A) is
// not needed here: the domain stops at PI/A and does not go all the way round,
// so A can be any real > 0 and the surface stays regular. Larger A = more
// tightly wound spiral = more twisted band.
//
// NORMALIZATION. The shader uses v in [0,1] with phi = v*PI/A: then
//     r = A*phi/2 = v*PI/2
// and r NO LONGER depends on A. This is why the band always has the same
// two edges (r goes from 0 to PI/2 whatever A is): A changes ONLY how much the
// surface winds, not where it starts and ends.
//
// --- FIXED 4D ROTATION (avoids the stereographic clamp) ---
// The edge C34 passes through the projection pole w = +1: there stereoS3
// saturates (rad = min(sqrt((1+w)/(1-w)), 12)) and the edge would come out cut
// -- the known limit documented in the Hopf tori presets. Measured: max w = 1.000000
// and 1.62% of the vertices above 0.95.
// A FIXED rigid rotation in the (x1, x4) plane by 0.6 rad brings the maximum to
// w = 0.825 and the vertices above 0.95 to ZERO: the band is seen whole.
// It must mix x1 (or x2) with x4: a rotation in (x3, x4) is NOT enough, because
// C34 is a circle precisely in that plane and stays at w = 1 anyway (verified:
// 0.9998). The rotation is an isometry of S^3, so it deforms nothing.
//MESH_BEGIN
u: 0, 6.28318531, 400
v: 0, 1, 400
//MESH_END

// A = how much the spiral winds (turns around the axis between the two poles).
float Aa = max(A, 0.05);

// v normalized -> true angle on the base. r does not depend on A (see above).
float phi = v * 3.14159265 / Aa;
float r   = v * 1.57079633;

float cr = cos(r);
float sr = sin(r);

// Hopf lift: u runs ALONG THE FIBER, v along the base spiral.
float q1 = cr * cos(phi + u);
float q2 = cr * sin(phi + u);
float q3 = sr * cos(u);
float q4 = sr * sin(u);

// Fixed rotation in the (x1, x4) plane: moves the edge C34 away from the pole w = 1.
float ca = 0.82533561;   // cos(0.6)
float sa = 0.56464247;   // sin(0.6)

return vec4(
    ca * q1 - sa * q4,
    q2,
    q3,
    sa * q1 + ca * q4
);
